  "annotation_method": "Third held-out set. Written by reading the full criteria of each study after the Montreal fixes were merged and before the parser was run on these studies. Only lines with a reference rule are listed; every other line is expected to stay unknown. Not clinically reviewed.",
  "selection": "Third held-out set. For each condition, the first 4 studies in API order with a recruiting site in Ottawa, Canada, skipping any study in studies.json, vancouver.json, toronto.json, montreal.json or the demo trials (kept or dropped). Fetched after the Montreal fixes were merged, and labelled before the parser was run on them.",
  "scope": "A line gets a reference rule only if the whole line is one of: an age limit (wording that covers everyone, with age at consent or enrollment treated as current age); a sex limit; a named condition with no duration, severity, history, timing, treatment or alternative attached; or a single limit or inclusive range on hemoglobin, platelets, ANC, creatinine, HbA1c, BMI, eGFR or LVEF with no time window, method or other measurement attached. Lines nested under another line, in an unknown section, or next to an \"or\" get no rule. Conditions outside the parser vocabulary and abbreviations still count, so they show up as misses. Cohort-specific lines count as context-dependent. When a line has a self-contained part and a qualified part, only the self-contained part gets a rule. A source unit that looks wrong (eGFR per 1.72m2) gets no rule.",
  "method": "Held-out set: exact match on study, source offsets, section, field, operator, value, unit and qualifiers. The parser was not changed after these studies were fetched.",
